MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTE2NjAyNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2814#issuecomment-421166024"},"message":"By the way, git-annex and datalad are just... in a word... awesome. These are tools that need to be used / embraced and integrated into daily life because it's by time we have better organization and definition of data and not \"the land of the lost scratch space on sherlock where I have no idea where my graduate school data went to be created and die.\"","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1536877025,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTE3MDU3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2814#issuecomment-421170572"},"message":"@satra could you help Vanessa to get rid of her illegal status on neurostars? See above https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2814#issuecomment-421152303\n\nPS I guess it is my bad influence which makes my friends inadmissable to sacred places","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1536877200,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTE3MTE2NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2814#issuecomment-421171165"},"message":"crawler is just to automate generation and updates of the datasets from websites and databases like xnat. It is just an addition/extension now, although was the seed for the entire datalad Enterprise - to make available datasets under git/git-annex. That is how we couldn't produce and update those hundreds of datasets we have already.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"3286e9a6aeeb25e1bf3fcf613be9da3d3270e55d"},"timestamp":1536877368,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTE3MTcxOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2814#issuecomment-421171719"},"message":"Ohh so crawler is like... more controlled and packaged corn job to sync things?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1536877667,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTE3MjY1Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2814#issuecomment-421172657"},"message":"There are multiple ways metadata could be stored, provided. Eg you can assign arbitrary simple key/value pairs and tags using git-annex metadata command which will store it within git-annex branch.\nThen metadata could be extracted from various files and datasets stored in various formats (PDF, exif in jpeg, bids, etc and also those simple ones stored in git annex branch as I noted above) and placed into files to be kept under git or git-annex. That is the purpose of various metadata extractors in datalad, which are used by datalad aggregate-metadata, which also collects them from subdatasets. Then the topmost superdataset ends up having access to all such aggregated metadata, and you can `datalad search` (did you try it already?) to locate specific datasets and files which might not even yet be installed.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1536877765,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTE3Mjk3MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2814#issuecomment-421172971"},"message":"crawler - yeah, it is a tool you could put on a Cron job ;-) We rerun it manually from time to time ATM","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1536877799,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTE3MzA1MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2814#issuecomment-421173051"},"message":"It is now like git pull ;-)","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1536877799,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDEyOTc5ODU0Mw=="},"target":"434b841621069833bf251d3d749a20a0b9b4f460eac94e107dcfa54ec694af4a","message":"It is  like   git pull ;-)","